# Dialog Window Standards

Related: [tailwind-css.mdc](tailwind-css.mdc) (mobile-first, tokens), [front-end-structure.mdc](front-end-structure.mdc) (feature folders). Implementation: [`CustomDialog.tsx`](../../ui-kit/package/src/components/CustomDialog.tsx).

Reference implementations: `DialogsPage.tsx` (`NestedDialogDemo` — stacked siblings), `ProfileMediaSelectorModal.tsx` (consumer + iframe crop), `CreateFolderDialog.tsx`, `ThemeDeleteDialog.tsx`.

## Which dialog to use

| Use | Component |
|-----|-----------|
| Forms, wizards, selection, previews, delete (sized) | **`CustomDialog`** from `@webonone/ui-kit` |
| Strict non-dismissible destructive confirm | **`AlertDialog`** |
| Low-level Radix composition | UI Kit internals only — not feature code |

## Core layout

- Build with **`CustomDialog`**; do not use raw `Dialog` primitives in features when `CustomDialog` applies.
- Every dialog: visible **header** + visible **footer**.
- Global actions (Cancel, Save, Submit, Delete, Next, Previous, **Crop & Upload**) go in the **`footer` prop only** — never in the body.
- This applies to **stacked inner dialogs** and **consumer-hosted embed dialogs** — if the consumer renders `CustomDialog`, the iframe/embed child must not duplicate footer actions.
- `CustomDialog` footer is already `flex justify-end gap-2`. Pass buttons as a fragment. No `w-full` / `flex-1` on footer buttons unless explicitly required.

## Footer buttons

- Uniform height: **`h-10`** on all footer actions in the same dialog.
- **Cancel:** `variant="outline"`, `className="h-10 px-4 border-[hsl(var(--glass-border))] text-foreground hover:bg-accent"`.
- **Primary (Save/Create):** `variant="default"`, `h-10`, Lucide `Save` with `className="mr-2 h-4 w-4"` before the label.
- **Destructive:** `variant="destructive"`, `h-10`, `Trash2` icon when appropriate.
- Form dialogs: Zod + `FormField` in body per [form-creation skill](../skills/form-creation/SKILL.md).

## Sizing (quick reference)

| Use case | `sizeWidth` × `sizeHeight` |
|----------|---------------------------|
| Simple form | `small` × `medium` or `auto` |
| Long form / lists | `small` × `large` |
| Selection | `medium` × `large` |
| Wizard | `large` × `xlarge` |
| Delete / short confirm | `auto` + `maxWidth="max-w-md"` |

**Width presets:** `small` 50%, `medium` 66%, `large` 75%, `xlarge` 83%, `auto` + `maxWidth`. **Height presets:** `small` 33%, `medium` 50%, `large` 75%, `xlarge` 90%, `auto` content-sized. Shell always `max-h-[calc(100vh-1rem)]`. Omitted `sizeHeight` defaults to `sizeWidth` (or `auto` when `sizeWidth="auto"`).

**Scroll:** fixed height → body `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`; `disableContentScroll` → `overflow-hidden` for internal scroll (iframes, crop).

### CustomDialog props (common)

| Prop | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `nestedDismissGuard` | Blocks overlay/focus/Escape dismiss while inner dialog open (extend with post-close buffer — see stacked section) |
| `stackLevel` | Stacked sibling z-index (`100 + level * 10`); inner dialog uses `1` or higher |
| `noContentPadding` | Full-bleed body (media iframe) |
| `disableContentScroll` | Body does not scroll; children manage overflow |
| `hideCloseButton` | Delete-style confirms |
| `maxWidth` | With `sizeWidth="auto"`, caps width; with percent presets, optional `sm:{maxWidth}` override |

Optional Radix passthrough on content: `onInteractOutside`, `onPointerDownOutside`, `onFocusOutside`, `onEscapeKeyDown`. When `nestedDismissGuard` is true, dismiss events are prevented before custom handlers run.

## Padding and theme

- Do not fight shell padding; use `noContentPadding` only for full-bleed body (e.g. media iframe).
- Body spacing: `space-y-*` — avoid conflicting nested `p-*`.
- Shell uses **`glass-card`** — do not replace with ad-hoc gradient/solid backgrounds.
- Inner cards/sections: `bg-[hsl(var(--glass-bg))]` + `border-[hsl(var(--glass-border))]`.
- Inputs: `bg-[hsl(var(--input-background))]`, `border-[hsl(var(--glass-border))]`, `text-foreground`.
- Typography: titles `text-foreground`; supporting copy `text-muted-foreground`.

## File structure

- One dialog per file: `features/<module>/components/<Name>Dialog.tsx`.
- Schemas in `features/<module>/schemas/` (not in the dialog file).

## Wizard dialogs

- One step component per step — no one long inline block.
- Single **step progress bar** only (`w-1/2 mx-auto`) — no duplicate numeric stepper.
- Next/Previous in footer.

## Tabbed dialogs

- One tab body component per tab.
- Tab-scoped actions (Add, Edit selected) in tab body; global actions in footer.
- Row actions via kebab (`MoreVertical`) per [item-list skill](../skills/item-list/SKILL.md).

## Stacked sibling dialogs

When a second dialog opens from an open dialog, use **sibling** `CustomDialog` instances in the **same document** — never render the inner dialog as a **child** of the outer dialog body.

### Required pattern

1. **Sibling JSX** — outer and inner are siblings under a fragment (`<>...</>`), not parent/child in the tree.
2. **Outer guard** — `nestedDismissGuard={innerOpen || blockOuterDismiss}` on the outer dialog (see **Inner close must not dismiss outer**).
3. **Inner stack** — `stackLevel={1}` on the inner dialog (+1 per additional layer).
4. **Dismiss order** — outer `onOpenChange(false)` while inner is open: close inner first, keep outer open (`useRef` + optional state guard).

Simple uncontrolled reference: [`NestedDialogDemo`](ui-kit/showcase/src/pages/DialogsPage.tsx). **Controlled outer** (parent owns `open` / `onClose`): [`ProfileMediaSelectorModal.tsx`](identity/frontend/src/features/profile/components/ProfileMediaSelectorModal.tsx).

### Inner close must not dismiss outer

When the inner dialog closes on button click, the pointer can **fall through** to the outer overlay and trigger outer `onOpenChange(false)` — closing both dialogs.

1. **`closeInnerDialog()` helper** — closes inner state only; never calls parent `onClose()` / `setOuterOpen(false)`.
2. **`innerOpenRef`** — sync from `innerOpen` in `useEffect` only; set `innerOpenRef.current = true` when **opening** inner; **never** set it `false` inside inner close handlers.
3. **Post-close dismiss buffer** — `blockOuterDismiss` state + ref; set `true` in `closeInnerDialog()`, clear after ~150ms (`setTimeout`, clear on unmount).
4. **Extended outer guard** — `nestedDismissGuard={innerOpen || blockOuterDismiss}` (not `innerOpen` alone).
5. **Outer `onOpenChange(false)`** — return without closing outer when `innerOpen`, `innerOpenRef.current`, or `blockOuterDismiss` / ref is true; call `closeInnerDialog()` if inner still open; only then call parent `onClose()`.
6. **Inner Cancel** — `type="button"`, `event.stopPropagation()`, call `closeInnerDialog()` directly.

### Anti-patterns

- Inner `CustomDialog` inside outer `CustomDialog` `children` (legacy: `ThemeCreateDialog` — migrate to siblings).
- Stacked dialog **inside an iframe** when the parent dialog is in the consumer window — `stackLevel` cannot overlay the parent modal; delegate via postMessage (`webonone:media:crop-request` → sibling inner dialog + `MediaCropDialogFrame` in parent document).
- Clearing `innerOpenRef` synchronously when inner closes → outer guard fails on async `onOpenChange`.
- `nestedDismissGuard={innerOpen}` without post-close buffer → pointer click-through dismisses outer.
- Calling parent `onClose()` from inner Cancel or inner `onOpenChange`.

### Skeleton (controlled outer + embed inner)

```tsx
const [innerOpen, setInnerOpen] = useState(false)
const [blockOuterDismiss, setBlockOuterDismiss] = useState(false)
const blockOuterDismissRef = useRef(false)
const innerOpenRef = useRef(false)

useEffect(() => { innerOpenRef.current = innerOpen }, [innerOpen])

const closeInnerDialog = useCallback(() => {
  setInnerOpen(false)
  blockOuterDismissRef.current = true
  setBlockOuterDismiss(true)
  window.setTimeout(() => {
    blockOuterDismissRef.current = false
    setBlockOuterDismiss(false)
  }, 150)
}, [])

function handleOuterOpenChange(next: boolean) {
  if (next) return
  if (innerOpen || innerOpenRef.current) { closeInnerDialog(); return }
  if (blockOuterDismissRef.current || blockOuterDismiss) return
  onClose() // parent-controlled outer only
}

return (
  <>
    <CustomDialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={handleOuterOpenChange} nestedDismissGuard={innerOpen || blockOuterDismiss} ... />
    <CustomDialog open={innerOpen} onOpenChange={(next) => !next && closeInnerDialog()} stackLevel={1}
      footer={<Button type="button" onClick={(e) => { e.stopPropagation(); closeInnerDialog() }}>Cancel</Button>} ... />
  </>
)
```

See **Iframe embed bodies** below when inner dialog hosts a media iframe.

## Iframe embed bodies (`noContentPadding`)

When a `CustomDialog` body hosts a Media (or other) iframe, the **consumer owns the dialog shell** — title, description, and **all** footer actions.

### Required pattern

1. **Footer in consumer only** — Cancel + primary (e.g. Crop & Upload) in host `footer` with `h-10` classes; domain widgets use `embedded` prop (`ImageCropDialog`) — **no** faux footer (`border-t` + Cancel/Submit) in iframe body.
2. **Confirm via postMessage** — primary footer calls `sendMediaConfirm(iframe, mediaOrigin)`; embed listens with `useMediaParentCommands` ([`CropDialogPage.tsx`](media/frontend/src/features/media/pages/CropDialogPage.tsx)).
3. **Height — consumer** — body wrapper `flex h-full min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden`; iframe `h-full min-h-0 w-full flex-1 border-0`.
4. **Height — embed document** — [`useEmbedDocumentFill`](media/frontend/src/features/media/hooks/useEmbedDocumentFill.ts) on embed pages; [`EmbedLayout`](media/frontend/src/features/media/components/EmbedLayout.tsx) chromeless uses **`h-dvh min-h-0`** (`h-full` alone breaks when `#root` → React tree does not propagate height).
5. **Height — crop UI** — embedded crop body: CSS grid `grid-rows-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto]` (cropper + zoom); do not rely on bare `flex-1` cropper without a resolved height chain.

### Forbidden in embed iframe content

- Button rows styled as dialog footers; `CustomDialog` inside iframe when parent provides the shell
- Duplicating footer actions in consumer footer and iframe body
- `flex-1` cropper without `h-dvh` / grid → cropper collapses (only zoom slider visible)

Reference: [`ProfileMediaSelectorModal.tsx`](identity/frontend/src/features/profile/components/ProfileMediaSelectorModal.tsx), [`CropDialogPage.tsx`](media/frontend/src/features/media/pages/CropDialogPage.tsx).

## Responsive / mobile-first

**Shell (built into `CustomDialog` — do not override):** outer padding `px-2 py-2` → `sm:px-4 sm:py-4`; `max-h-[calc(100vh-1rem)]`; `maxWidth` overrides use `w-full sm:{maxWidth}`; body scroll per height preset.

**Sizing on mobile:** prefer `auto` + `maxWidth` for short confirms; percent presets apply at all breakpoints — do not assume desktop-only widths; no fixed `px` shell widths.

**Body content:** mobile-first single column; columns at `md:` / `lg:` only (e.g. `grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2`). No horizontal overflow; `min-w-0` on flex/grid children. Full-width inputs on phone. Wizard bar stays `w-1/2 mx-auto`.

**Footer on narrow screens:** wrap long footers in `<div className="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-end gap-2">`; keep `h-10` touch targets; no full-width stacked buttons unless required.

See [tailwind-css.mdc](tailwind-css.mdc) for breakpoint conventions.

## Verification

```bash
npm run type-check -w webonone-v2-root   # or media-root / identity-root
npm run build -w @webonone/ui-kit        # when touching CustomDialog
```

Manual (stacked + embed crop):

1. Open outer → trigger inner (e.g. upload image) → **Cancel on inner** → inner closes, **outer stays open**.
2. Crop: image fills crop area; zoom below cropper; **no** action buttons in iframe body; **Crop & Upload** in consumer footer only.
3. Escape / overlay on outer while inner open → inner closes first, outer remains.

Manual (responsive): ~375px / ~320px — no clipped footer, no body horizontal scroll; long titles wrap.
